    <entry>
        <title>I Wake and Feel the Fell of Dark, Not Day</title>
        <author>
            <name>Jujube</name>
        </author>
        <link href="https://www.jujubemonster.com/i-wake-and-feel-the-fell-of-dark-not-day.html"/>
        <id>https://www.jujubemonster.com/i-wake-and-feel-the-fell-of-dark-not-day.html</id>
        <media:content url="https://www.jujubemonster.com/media/posts/160/abstractalien-2.png" medium="image" />
            <category term="poetry"/>

        <updated>2026-09-30T09:05:41-07:00</updated>
            <summary type="html">
                <![CDATA[
                        <img src="https://www.jujubemonster.com/media/posts/160/abstractalien-2.png" alt="scared and shocked face, collage, modern art" />
                    I am gall, I am heartburn. God's most deep decree Bitter would have me taste: my taste was me; Bones built in me, flesh filled, blood brimmed the curse. Selfyeast of spirit a dull dough sours. I see The lost are like this, and their&hellip;
                ]]>
            </summary>
        <content type="html">
            <![CDATA[
                    <p><img src="https://www.jujubemonster.com/media/posts/160/abstractalien-2.png" class="type:primaryImage" alt="scared and shocked face, collage, modern art" /></p>
                <p>I am gall, I am heartburn. God's most deep decree<br>Bitter would have me taste: my taste was me;<br>Bones built in me, flesh filled, blood brimmed the curse.<br><br>Selfyeast of spirit a dull dough sours. I see <br>The lost are like this, and their scourge to be<br>As I am mine, their sweating selves, but worse. </p>
<p>-- Gerard Manley Hopkins (1844 –1889)</p>
<figure class="post__image"><img loading="lazy"  src="https://www.jujubemonster.com/media/posts/160/abstractalien.png" alt="" width="500" height="663"></figure>
            ]]>
        </content>
